[6:33PM] #Alausa_Ikeja #TrafficUpdate 

Fluid traffic movement on Obafemi Awolowo Way, spanning from Barrack, Coca-Cola Junction, Radio, Allen Junction to Balogun, facilitating a seamless commute.
Congested traffic from Olowu to Ikeja underneath the bridge, precipitated by spillover from the Ikeja Along overpass, necessitating caution and patience.
Measured traffic progression on the return journey from Olowu, Allen Junction to Radio, attributed to the systematic alternation of traffic lights.
Unimpeded movement on Lateef Jakande Road from Coca-Cola Junction to Cadbury, ensuring a smooth journey.
Traffic congestion observed from Cadbury, First Gate, Wemco Junction to Omole Roundabout, whereas the return journey is proceeding without major impediments.
Busy traffic conditions on Aromire onward Adeniyi Jones, Akora Villa to Hacco, with the return journey experiencing congestion approaching Allen Junction.

Notably, Acme Road has been reopened for vehicular movement from Mobolaji Johnson Avenue to Alausa Intersection, and the stretch of Dr. Nurudeen Olowopopo connecting to Otedola underneath the bridge remains in optimal condition.

